      "writtenOn": "2024-12-03T06:53:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The new code makes the problem worse though, because an older, lower value may be cached for a long time after higher values were returned.\n\nFor example:\n\n - [Thread1] statsFetcher.get() --\u003e returns 42\n - [Thread2] statsFetcher.get() --\u003e returns 43\n - [Thread2] Caches 43\n - [Thread1] Caches 42\n --\u003e Anyone from that point gets 42 for a few seconds. Before, it would only return 42 on the calls that raced, the value wouldn\u0027t remain in cache.\n\nI think this can be fixed by replacing `void cache.put()` with `StatsResult cache.putIfAbsent()`, which would return the currently cached value if any. Then this method would return the value that was put into the cache, so the flow becomes:\n\n - [Thread1] statsFetcher.get() --\u003e returns 42\n - [Thread2] statsFetcher.get() --\u003e returns 43\n - [Thread2] Caches 43\n - [Thread1] putIfAbsent(42) -\u003e returns 43 --\u003e method returns 43",
